    "faqSection": {
      "title": "FAQ",
      "contactInfo": "Can`t find what you`re looking for? Connect with our team at hello@hackutd.co",
      "callToAction": {
        "text": "Ask A Question!",
        "link": "mailto:hello@hackutd.co"
      },
      "questions": [
        {
          "question": "What is a hackathon?",
          "answer": "A hackathon is a 24-hour competition where you and up to 3 teammates build a software project from scratch and compete against other groups for prizes. Sponsors will also provide workshops, events, and activities throughout the weekend to help you learn more about the field of technology!"
        },
        {
          "question": "Where will it be?",
          "answer": "HackUTD will be hosted at... You guessed it: UT Dallas! Parking and other logistical details for attendees will be provided closer to the hackathon date."
        },
        {
          "question": "Does HackUTD cover travel?",
          "answer": "HackUTD does do travel reimbursement! Check our policies here!"
        },
        {
          "question": "Can I participate if I have never hacked?",
          "answer": "Everyone is welcome to come, and no experience is necessary to attend! We will even be hosting workshops to introduce new hackers to industry programs and technologies."
        },
        {
          "question": "When do applications close?",
          "answer": "Applications will close on October 18th."
        },
        {
          "question": "What do I need to bring?",
          "answer": "You just need to bring a laptop, charger, and a hacking spirit to participate! We also recommend having a compiler, packages, or any packaging tools ready beforehand. We will be providing internet connectivity, and will also have free food throughout the event!"
        },
        {
          "question": "What should I build?",
          "answer": "Anything you want! You can try to solve a sponsor challenge or submit a project for the HackUTD awards!"
        },
        {
          "question": "Does HackUTD accept walk-ins?",
          "answer": "Historically HackUTD has taken limited walk-ins. We anticipate to take walk-ins again this year but will be subject to venue capacity!"
        },
        {
          "question": "When is HackUTD 2025?",
          "answer": "November 8th and 9th!"
        },
        {
          "question": "Free swag? pls?",
          "answer": "We will have custom HackUTD 2025 swag for all participants along with gear provided by our sponsors! And free food!"
        },
        {
          "question": "What if I don't have a team?",
          "answer": "We will have a team building session at the start of the hackathon for those who need help finding one! You can also choose to work on projects by yourself."
        },
        {
          "question": "How much does it cost?",
          "answer": "HackUTD 2025 will be completely free to hackers!"
        },
        {
          "question": "What are the general rules?",
          "answer": "Your project must be built entirely over the course of the weekend. No previous projects or code may be used. Have fun! Your behavior at this event is subject to the MLH Code of Conduct as well as any applicable UT Dallas guidelines."
        },
        {
          "question": "Can I volunteer?",
          "answer": "Mentor and volunteer applications will be opening soon! Follow us on social media to be notified when applications open."
        }
      ]
    },
